 "answer": "The air quality is better in the **north** of Singapore compared to the west. \n\nHowever, due to ongoing regional haze, the air quality across the entire island remains in the **Unhealthy** range (PSI between 101 and 200). \n\nBased on monitoring data from the National Environment Agency (NEA) and air quality trackers:\n* **North:** More favorable, with PSI/AQI readings hovering around **124 to 164**. \n* **West:** Significantly more polluted, with readings reaching around **182 to 187**.\n\nIf you are planning immediate outdoor activities, it is advisable to minimize prolonged or strenuous exertion in both regions and check the NEA's hourly PM2.5 readings for the most immediate localized shifts.",
